INFRA showed us, that a long time ago- things got left behind when projects and companies failed.

In Obensuer, it was a small analog TV station.

As Obenseuer became a dumping ground and then a quarantine sector, the TV station found new life as pirate TV station.
At first it was rants and/or conspiracy theories to camera, a public soapbox for the loudest most dedicated indiviuals to stand on. The most entertaining to watch survived.

Authorites took a while to notice it- an analog station when the world had switched to digital? Who even watched analog tv anymore?
Crazies and Shroomheads, and some that just wanteed the classic snow and white noise.
The station was word-of-mouth or randomly stumbled upon.

In the lead-up to digital tv, people brought converters to allow analog tvs to play digital signals- in Obenseuer you can find the opposite- hand-made boxes to let digital tvs to plau analog signals.

Pirate TV, the government could have shut it down, but just chose to impose a few rules instead. After all- it kept the smarter indiviuals busy running the station or scrounging and makingg converter boxes, and the dumber ones glued to the TV, with programming that appealed to their shroom and alchohol muddled minds that standard TV didn't always fulfill.
